WEBVTT

00:02:12.824 --> 00:02:14.101
Hey,  Maddie.

00:02:14.104 --> 00:02:16.590
Listen, I, uh, hate to pull you away,

00:02:16.593 --> 00:02:19.277
But I'm gonna need you to come
back to the office with me.

00:02:19.315 --> 00:02:20.881
Really?

00:02:20.884 --> 00:02:24.781
Yeah, it turns out I got to
file those docs by midnight.

00:02:24.784 --> 00:02:28.331
I'm gonna need you to, um...

00:02:30.774 --> 00:02:32.741
This isn't working at all, is it?

00:02:32.744 --> 00:02:34.211
No, it's not, Nate.

00:02:34.214 --> 00:02:35.381
Listen, I've had a couple.

00:02:35.584 --> 00:02:37.261
I shouldn't really drive.

00:02:37.564 --> 00:02:40.291
Could you just give me a lift
--  I already called you a cab.

00:02:41.914 --> 00:02:43.671
I'll see you in the morning.

00:02:51.384 --> 00:02:52.711
Does that happen a lot?

00:02:52.714 --> 00:02:55.021
Only on the days that end with a Y.

00:03:05.974 --> 00:03:06.761
You okay?

00:03:08.004 --> 00:03:08.981
Yeah.

00:03:12.724 --> 00:03:14.021
I've got to go.

00:05:10.764 --> 00:05:12.481
Here is the detective

00:05:19.384 --> 00:05:20.701
That's a pretty nasty bite.

00:05:21.504 --> 00:05:22.611
You know what bit him?

00:05:22.614 --> 00:05:25.321
I haven't quite
determined that just yet.

00:05:26.804 --> 00:05:27.811
Come on, doc.

00:05:27.814 --> 00:05:29.211
Off the record.

00:05:30.024 --> 00:05:33.381
Okay, way, way off the record.

00:05:33.974 --> 00:05:37.491
If I didn't know better, I'd say
the guy was attacked by a wolf.

00:05:37.494 --> 00:05:41.271
But unless I know that the zoo is missing
one of their lobos, I'm going with pit bull.

00:05:41.274 --> 00:05:42.941
I like my job.

00:05:42.944 --> 00:05:44.131
Yeah, I hear you.

00:05:44.134 --> 00:05:45.131
One more thing.

00:05:45.134 --> 00:05:47.931
This guy -Was his heart missing?

00:05:49.044 --> 00:05:50.261
Yeah, how did you know that?

00:05:50.264 --> 00:05:51.791
I haven't even finished my report.

00:05:51.794 --> 00:05:53.311
Lucky guess.

00:05:57.654 --> 00:06:00.171
This lawyer guy first
heart-Free corpse in town?

00:06:00.174 --> 00:06:01.431
First man.

00:06:01.704 --> 00:06:03.861
Over the past year, several
women have gone missing.

00:06:04.584 --> 00:06:09.261
Dead bodies all washed up later in the bay,
too deteriorated to draw firm conclusions.

00:06:09.264 --> 00:06:11.511
But no hearts. No hearts

00:06:11.554 --> 00:06:13.271
They were all hookers
working at hunter's point.

00:06:13.274 --> 00:06:15.066
Cops are trying to
keep things under wrap,

00:06:15.069 --> 00:06:18.681
But they're looking for a serial
killer. And the lunar cycle?

00:06:18.684 --> 00:06:22.081
Yeah, month after month, all the murders
happened in the week leading up to the full moon.

00:06:22.084 --> 00:06:24.351
Which is this week. There is the lawer

00:06:24.354 --> 00:06:25.601
Awesome.

00:06:26.954 --> 00:06:29.141
Dean, could you be a
bigger geek about this?

00:06:29.144 --> 00:06:31.385
I'm sorry, man, but what
about a human by day,

00:06:31.388 --> 00:06:34.423
A freak animal killing machine
by moonlight don't you understand?

00:06:34.426 --> 00:06:38.068
We haven't seen one since we were kids.

00:06:38.294 --> 00:06:39.561
Okay, sparky.

00:06:39.874 --> 00:06:40.861
Then you know what?

00:06:40.864 --> 00:06:43.996
After we kill it, we can go to disneyland.
Know what the best part about it is?

00:06:43.999 --> 00:06:48.119
We already know how to
bring these suckers down.

00:06:48.814 --> 00:06:50.021
So what's our next move?

00:06:50.024 --> 00:06:51.871
Talk to the girl who found the body.

00:06:53.644 --> 00:06:54.661
Madison: I don't understand.

00:06:54.664 --> 00:06:56.101
I already gave my statement to you.

00:06:56.104 --> 00:06:58.581
Well, we just need to
verify a few things.

00:06:58.584 --> 00:07:01.781
This is my neighbor glenn.
Glenn, this is detective...

00:07:01.784 --> 00:07:04.067
Landis. And detective dante.

00:07:04.105 --> 00:07:06.241
Well, guess I'll leave you to it.

00:07:09.068 --> 00:07:09.782
Okay.

00:07:09.785 --> 00:07:11.241
Thanks for the casserole.

00:07:12.314 --> 00:07:13.481
Oh, how thoughtful.

00:07:13.954 --> 00:07:15.671
Just call if you need anything.

00:07:18.304 --> 00:07:19.181
He's sweet.

00:07:19.184 --> 00:07:21.081
He came over to check on me.

00:07:21.604 --> 00:07:23.331
Have a seat.

00:07:29.054 --> 00:07:30.791
You must be pretty shaken up.

00:07:31.474 --> 00:07:33.461
You were nate mulligan's
assistant, right?

00:07:33.464 --> 00:07:34.461
For two years, yeah.

00:07:34.464 --> 00:07:36.151
So you knew all about him.

00:07:36.154 --> 00:07:38.441
Probably knew more
about him than he did.

00:07:38.444 --> 00:07:39.451
Nate was...

00:07:39.814 --> 00:07:41.061
He was nice.

00:07:42.194 --> 00:07:44.441
But...

00:07:44.444 --> 00:07:47.865
You get a few scotches in him, and he
started hitting on anyone in a 5-Miles radius.

00:07:47.868 --> 00:07:49.811
You know the type.

00:07:53.484 --> 00:07:56.221
Yeah. I do, actually.

00:07:56.894 --> 00:07:59.521
Did, uh, did he have any
enemies? What do you mean?

00:07:59.524 --> 00:08:01.318
Sure looked like an animal attack.

00:08:01.321 --> 00:08:03.571
We're just covering all the bases.

00:08:03.574 --> 00:08:04.794
Anyone that might have
had a beef with him

00:08:04.797 --> 00:08:07.542
Former client, an ex. What?

00:08:07.545 --> 00:08:09.199
Well, this is embarrassing,

00:08:09.202 --> 00:08:10.927
But my ex-Boyfriend, kurt.

00:08:10.930 --> 00:08:12.494
Kurt have a last name? Mueller

00:08:12.532 --> 00:08:14.441
After we broke up, he went kind of nuts.

00:08:14.444 --> 00:08:15.601
He's...

00:08:15.944 --> 00:08:18.021
Well, he's kind of been stalking me.

00:08:18.024 --> 00:08:21.231
He got it in his head that something
was going on between Nate and I.

00:08:21.234 --> 00:08:22.821
He showed up at my office.

00:08:22.824 --> 00:08:24.638
And what happened? Kurt
got into it with nate.

00:08:24.641 --> 00:08:27.610
Threw a punch before security grabbed
him. I was lucky to keep my job.

00:08:27.613 --> 00:08:28.871
When was the last time you saw kurt?

00:08:28.874 --> 00:08:29.971
A few nights ago.

00:08:29.974 --> 00:08:31.641
Actually, the night Nate died.

00:08:31.644 --> 00:08:34.431
We were all grabbing drinks at
this bar, and Kurt showed up.

00:08:34.434 --> 00:08:35.271
And?

00:08:35.274 --> 00:08:36.191
Nothing.

00:08:36.794 --> 00:08:37.791
It was...

00:08:37.794 --> 00:08:39.831
Like he was watching me.

00:08:39.834 --> 00:08:41.321
Then he was gone.

00:08:41.324 --> 00:08:42.751
Tell you the truth...

00:08:43.444 --> 00:08:45.111
He scares me.

00:08:47.694 --> 00:08:48.871
So, what do you think?

00:08:48.874 --> 00:08:50.951
Stalker ex-Boyfriend.

00:08:50.954 --> 00:08:52.191
He hates the boss.

00:08:52.194 --> 00:08:53.441
And he was there that night.

00:08:53.444 --> 00:08:54.841
Think he's our dog-Faced boy?

00:08:55.104 --> 00:08:56.981
Well, it's a theory.

00:08:57.734 --> 00:08:58.931
We've had worse.

00:08:59.554 --> 00:09:02.101
What do you say we pay kurt a visit?

00:10:27.654 --> 00:10:30.121
Nothing but leftovers and a six-Pack.

00:10:30.604 --> 00:10:31.831
Check the freezer.

00:10:31.834 --> 00:10:35.211
Maybe there's some human hearts
behind the haagen-Dazs or something.

00:11:01.434 --> 00:11:02.661
Sam, come here.

00:11:08.154 --> 00:11:09.491
Check it out.

00:11:21.174 --> 00:11:22.501
Somebody there?

00:11:53.754 --> 00:11:55.541
I'll call 911.

00:12:03.214 --> 00:12:05.931
I'd say Kurt's looking
more and more like our cujo.

00:12:05.934 --> 00:12:08.891
If he's out here, we
better check on Madison.

00:12:13.634 --> 00:12:14.651
What's going on?

00:12:14.654 --> 00:12:16.671
Police business, glenn.

00:12:18.614 --> 00:12:19.831
What is it?

00:12:21.714 --> 00:12:24.231
Well, maybe we should talk privately?

00:12:24.854 --> 00:12:26.421
Has kurt been here?

00:12:26.424 --> 00:12:28.161
Not exactly.

00:12:28.604 --> 00:12:31.241
What exactly does "not exactly" mean?

00:12:31.244 --> 00:12:35.531
Well, he was outside
last night -Just looking.

00:12:35.534 --> 00:12:37.771
Just looking at me.

00:12:38.154 --> 00:12:39.851
Has he done something?

00:12:39.854 --> 00:12:42.501
We're not really sure.
It's probably nothing.

00:12:42.504 --> 00:12:43.581
But...

00:12:43.584 --> 00:12:44.921
We just don't want to take any chances.

00:12:44.924 --> 00:12:47.093
In fact, one of us should
probably stay here with you,

00:12:47.096 --> 00:12:48.823
Just in case he stops by.

00:12:49.104 --> 00:12:51.451
Where does he work? He owns a body shop.

00:12:51.587 --> 00:12:54.371
You mind grabbing that
address for us? Thanks.

00:12:56.224 --> 00:12:59.261
All right, you go.I'll stay.
You go after the creepy ex.

00:12:59.264 --> 00:13:00.561
I'm gonna hang here with the hot chick.

00:13:00.564 --> 00:13:02.791
Why do you always get to
hang out with the girls?

00:13:02.794 --> 00:13:04.221
Because I'm older.

00:13:04.794 --> 00:13:07.781
No, screw that. We settle
this the old-Fashioned way.

00:13:14.094 --> 00:13:15.951
Dean, always with the scissors.

00:13:15.954 --> 00:13:18.381
Shut up. Shut up. Two out of three.

00:13:22.414 --> 00:13:22.814
God!

00:13:22.914 --> 00:13:24.601
Bundle up out there, all right?

00:13:46.394 --> 00:13:49.191
Um, do you want to sit on the
couch? No. No, no, I'm okay.

00:13:49.194 --> 00:13:51.951
It's more comfortable. Uh, I'm fine.

00:14:12.434 --> 00:14:15.121
You know, I think I
will sit on the couch.

00:14:28.844 --> 00:14:30.261
Let me guess.

00:14:30.264 --> 00:14:33.249
You're sitting on her couch trying
to think of something to say.

00:14:33.252 --> 00:14:34.977
Did you find kurt? He
hasn't been at work all week,

00:14:34.980 --> 00:14:38.183
But because I'm good, and
I mean really, really good,

00:14:38.186 --> 00:14:41.001
I got a line on where he might be.

00:14:42.924 --> 00:14:45.621
What's she wearing? Bye, dean.

00:14:48.644 --> 00:14:50.391
Oh, sammy.

00:15:01.054 --> 00:15:03.871
Who died and made you sheriff?
I will call who I want.

00:15:04.074 --> 00:15:07.611
Whatever you want. Look what time it is.

00:15:07.614 --> 00:15:10.501
You're gonna wake her up and start talking about
- I saw that.

00:15:10.504 --> 00:15:12.371
What? Saw what?

00:15:12.614 --> 00:15:13.947
Okay, this
is the deal --

00:15:13.950 --> 00:15:17.251
My house, my tv.

00:15:17.254 --> 00:15:19.408
I never get to watch my show,

00:15:19.411 --> 00:15:21.246
So suck it up.

00:15:33.664 --> 00:15:34.616
Wait, so

00:15:34.619 --> 00:15:38.845
So kindall married ethan's
father just to get back at him?

00:15:39.474 --> 00:15:42.381
And now she's set to inherit all the
casinos that were supposed to go to ethan.

00:15:42.384 --> 00:15:44.751
What a bitch!

00:15:47.334 --> 00:15:50.111
Admit it -You're hooked.
No, no, no, no, no, no.

00:15:50.114 --> 00:15:52.621
I wouldn't say I'm hooked.

00:15:55.844 --> 00:15:57.561
Can I ask you a question?

00:15:57.804 --> 00:16:00.771
It's ... it's a little personal.

00:16:00.774 --> 00:16:03.071
You've seen my entire
underwear collection.

00:16:03.074 --> 00:16:05.371
Go ahead.

00:16:05.374 --> 00:16:07.151
Okay, um...

00:16:07.774 --> 00:16:10.781
Well, you're -You're clearly smart.

00:16:10.784 --> 00:16:13.711
I mean, your house is full
of great books, you know?

00:16:13.714 --> 00:16:17.111
And you're independent. Uh-Huh.

00:16:18.104 --> 00:16:21.141
What were you doing with kurt?

00:16:22.684 --> 00:16:24.521
I don't know.

00:16:25.474 --> 00:16:27.435
I mean, it's not like he
introduced himself, like,

00:16:27.438 --> 00:16:30.204
Hi, I'm possessive and controlling,
and I like to punch people.

00:16:30.207 --> 00:16:32.980
Want to be my girlfriend?

00:16:32.983 --> 00:16:34.219
Yeah, well,

00:16:34.222 --> 00:16:35.995
I guess we all make mistakes.

00:16:35.998 --> 00:16:38.681
Yeah, well, mine's wanted by the police.

00:16:39.324 --> 00:16:42.411
You want to know why I
stayed with him? Really?

00:16:44.034 --> 00:16:46.071
I was too insecure to leave.

00:16:46.074 --> 00:16:49.421
Well, I find that hard to believe.
You don't really seem like the type.

00:16:49.424 --> 00:16:51.581
Yeah, well some stuff happened.

00:16:52.014 --> 00:16:54.551
My life changed, I changed,
for the better, I think.

00:16:54.554 --> 00:16:57.871
What happened? Well, for
one thing, I got mugged.

00:16:58.804 --> 00:17:00.791
And that's supposed to be a good thing?

00:17:00.794 --> 00:17:02.496
I know, it sounds strange,

00:17:02.499 --> 00:17:03.956
And don't get me
wrong -It rattled me --

00:17:03.959 --> 00:17:06.185
But then it hit me.

00:17:06.188 --> 00:17:11.241
I could keep feeling sorry for myself
or I could take control of my life.

00:17:11.244 --> 00:17:13.351
I chose the latter.

00:17:14.004 --> 00:17:15.921
First thing I did was
tell kurt he had to go.

00:17:15.924 --> 00:17:19.201
Smart move. Apparently.

00:17:19.204 --> 00:17:22.181
Everything else just
opened up, blossomed.

00:17:22.444 --> 00:17:24.341
It's all been wonderful, really.

00:17:25.114 --> 00:17:26.501
What?

00:17:28.324 --> 00:17:30.495
Doesn't everybody think that being
a victim of random violence is

00:17:30.498 --> 00:17:32.619
The best thing that
ever happened to them?

00:17:32.644 --> 00:17:34.701
Yeah, not so much.

00:17:38.124 --> 00:17:40.021
You're...

00:17:40.024 --> 00:17:41.751
Unusual.

00:17:43.384 --> 00:17:45.391
Unusual like...

00:17:45.764 --> 00:17:48.311
"Unusual"? No, no, no.

00:17:48.314 --> 00:17:51.241
Unusual like...

00:17:54.054 --> 00:17:55.841
Impressive.

00:17:59.634 --> 00:18:00.951
You think so?

00:18:05.914 --> 00:18:07.281
Sorry.

00:18:10.604 --> 00:18:12.500
Hey. I found him.

00:18:12.554 --> 00:18:14.811
Good. Don't take your eyes off him.

00:18:18.494 --> 00:18:20.371
Oh, yeah, my eyes are glued.

00:18:20.374 --> 00:18:22.351
Look, sammy, I got to let you go.

00:18:22.354 --> 00:18:24.961
I, uh, I don't want to miss anything.

00:18:35.344 --> 00:18:36.931
So, um...

00:18:37.634 --> 00:18:39.041
I'm gonna turn in.

00:18:39.044 --> 00:18:40.001
Okay, yeah.

00:18:40.004 --> 00:18:42.261
Well, I'll be here. Okay.

00:18:42.264 --> 00:18:47.401
If you hear anything, if you
wake up, just -Just call out.

00:18:50.144 --> 00:18:52.921
Okay. Okay.

00:20:24.914 --> 00:20:27.961
Dean, you okay? Yeah,
now that I'm conscious.

00:20:27.964 --> 00:20:29.821
The werewolf knocked me out.

00:20:29.824 --> 00:20:31.311
Sam, it's madison.

00:20:31.314 --> 00:20:32.401
What? !

00:20:32.404 --> 00:20:34.951
Yeah, awesome job of
keeping an eye on her.

00:20:39.364 --> 00:20:42.191
Dean, I've been here the whole
time. She's in bed asleep.

00:20:42.194 --> 00:20:43.511
Well, she wasn't an hour ago.

00:20:43.514 --> 00:20:47.101
Check her right arm. I nicked
her with a silver knife.

00:20:49.484 --> 00:20:50.861
Morning.

00:20:58.214 --> 00:21:00.721
Um, wherare my pajamas?

00:21:03.604 --> 00:21:05.251
Sam?

00:21:05.254 --> 00:21:07.271
What's going on?

00:21:09.274 --> 00:21:11.391
Where are you going?

00:21:11.394 --> 00:21:13.411
I'm not going anywhere.

00:21:13.414 --> 00:21:15.861
And neither are you.

00:21:22.474 --> 00:21:23.761
You're psychotic.

00:21:23.764 --> 00:21:26.671
The whole "I'm a cop"
trick. God, I am so stupid.

00:21:26.674 --> 00:21:29.001
Well, I guess neither of us
are who we said we were, huh?

00:21:29.004 --> 00:21:30.461
Sam, you're sick, okay?

00:21:30.464 --> 00:21:31.861
You're imagining things.

00:21:31.864 --> 00:21:34.391
Monsters don't exist. Not really.

00:21:34.394 --> 00:21:36.761
You know what? Save the act.

00:21:36.764 --> 00:21:38.701
It's not an act!

00:21:38.704 --> 00:21:42.331
I am not a werewolf!
There is no such thing!

00:21:42.334 --> 00:21:44.741
It's made up, all right?

00:21:44.744 --> 00:21:46.951
They're not real! You
know they're not real!

00:21:46.954 --> 00:21:48.811
No? Then where did that come from?

00:21:48.814 --> 00:21:50.181
I don't know!

00:21:50.594 --> 00:21:53.211
Sam, god, you need help.

00:21:53.824 --> 00:21:56.261
Please, don't do something
that you're gonna regret.

00:21:56.264 --> 00:21:58.951
I'm not what you think I am.

00:21:58.954 --> 00:22:00.671
I'm not.

00:22:12.864 --> 00:22:14.601
How you doing?

00:22:15.874 --> 00:22:18.241
My head feels great, thanks.

00:22:19.054 --> 00:22:20.661
We got to talk.

00:22:26.614 --> 00:22:28.691
She says she has no idea
what I'm talking about.

00:22:28.694 --> 00:22:29.841
She's lying.

00:22:30.274 --> 00:22:31.947
Maybe. Or maybe she really
doesn't know she's changing.

00:22:31.950 --> 00:22:34.881
Maybe when the creature
takes over, she blacks out.

00:22:34.884 --> 00:22:36.771
Like a really hot incredible hulk?

00:22:36.774 --> 00:22:40.091
Dude, she ganked her boss and her ex-Boyfriend.
That doesn't sound ration unconscious.

00:22:40.094 --> 00:22:41.641
But what if it was, dean?

00:22:41.644 --> 00:22:45.061
What if some animal part of her
brain saw both those guys as threats?

00:22:45.064 --> 00:22:47.481
Hell, the cop, too. Are
you the dog whisperer now?

00:22:47.484 --> 00:22:49.311
Look, man, I just...

00:22:50.354 --> 00:22:52.703
I don't know. There was
something in her eyes.

00:22:52.706 --> 00:22:53.738
Yeah, she's killing people.

00:22:53.741 --> 00:22:56.314
But if she has no control..
Exactly she can't control it.

00:22:56.318 --> 00:22:58.310
Even if she's telling the truth,
it's not gonna change anything.

00:22:58.313 --> 00:23:00.729
I'm not putting a bullet through some
girl who has no idea what's happening.

00:23:00.732 --> 00:23:02.299
Sam she is master You're
feeling sorry for her?

00:23:02.302 --> 00:23:04.161
Maybe I understand her.

00:23:06.254 --> 00:23:10.721
Look, there might be another way we can get
the job done without having to waste her.

00:23:15.674 --> 00:23:17.951
Are you thinking what
I think you're thinking?

00:23:18.694 --> 00:23:19.921
Dad's theory.

00:23:19.924 --> 00:23:24.201
Lycanthropy might have a cure if you kill the
werewolf who bit you, severing the bloodline.

00:23:24.204 --> 00:23:26.221
Might have a cure. Meaning who knows?

00:23:26.224 --> 00:23:28.521
It's worth a shot.  We don't
even know where to look.

00:23:28.984 --> 00:23:32.421
The puppy that bit her -- It could be
anyone, anywhere. Could have been years ago.

00:23:34.674 --> 00:23:36.601
No, I don't think so.

00:23:43.444 --> 00:23:44.501
Madison...

00:23:44.844 --> 00:23:46.751
When were you mugged?

00:23:48.434 --> 00:23:50.361
Please, it's important, all right?

00:23:50.364 --> 00:23:51.801
Just answer the question.

00:23:55.744 --> 00:23:57.721
About a month ago.

00:23:57.724 --> 00:23:59.551
Did you see the guy? No.

00:23:59.554 --> 00:24:00.901
He grabbed me from behind.

00:24:00.904 --> 00:24:02.481
Did he bite you?

00:24:06.644 --> 00:24:08.531
How did you know that?

00:24:09.644 --> 00:24:10.941
Where?

00:24:10.944 --> 00:24:13.051
O-On the back of my neck.

00:24:23.094 --> 00:24:24.631
Oh, that's just a love bite.

00:24:24.634 --> 00:24:27.131
Believe me, that could
have been a lot worse.

00:24:27.774 --> 00:24:30.971
Where were you at the time?
Walking home from a friend's loft.

00:24:30.974 --> 00:24:31.911
Let me guess.

00:24:32.424 --> 00:24:34.631
Not too far from hunter's point?

00:24:38.214 --> 00:24:40.381
Same place where those
other murders happened.

00:24:40.384 --> 00:24:42.831
I'm telling you, it's the
werewolf's hunting grounds.

00:24:44.214 --> 00:24:46.271
But that doesn't mean it's
gonna be out there tonight.

00:24:46.274 --> 00:24:47.981
It's the right time of the lunar cycle.

00:24:48.744 --> 00:24:50.801
I know it's a long shot.

00:24:50.804 --> 00:24:51.891
You're forgetting something.

00:24:51.894 --> 00:24:53.231
Maddie's probably gonna turn soon.

00:24:53.234 --> 00:24:55.711
We can't let her take off
to an all-You-Can-Eat buffet.

00:24:56.624 --> 00:24:57.881
I'll stay with her.

00:24:57.884 --> 00:24:59.481
And if she busts loose?

00:25:01.324 --> 00:25:02.835
Sam? I'll do it.

00:25:03.344 --> 00:25:05.871
Sam. I'll shoot her, all right?

00:25:06.684 --> 00:25:08.851
But, dean, I need you to go out there.

00:25:08.894 --> 00:25:10.331
At least go look for the thing.

00:25:10.334 --> 00:25:11.531
Dean, please.

00:25:11.534 --> 00:25:13.291
We can save this girl.

00:25:17.064 --> 00:25:18.351
Fine.

00:25:25.534 --> 00:25:27.141
Please.

00:25:28.574 --> 00:25:30.461
Just let me go.

00:25:55.304 --> 00:25:56.481
Look...

00:25:58.074 --> 00:26:00.271
I know you're scared.

00:26:00.274 --> 00:26:03.531
I also know that there's no way
in hell you're gonna believe me.

00:26:04.714 --> 00:26:06.671
But I'm doing this...

00:26:07.634 --> 00:26:10.111
Because I'm trying to help you.

00:26:11.224 --> 00:26:12.424
I'm not gonna lie, all right?

00:26:12.427 --> 00:26:14.911
The odds aren't exactly in our favor.

00:26:15.404 --> 00:26:20.621
But if this goes the
way I pray it does...

00:26:21.164 --> 00:26:22.689
I'll untie you,

00:26:23.613 --> 00:26:27.221
And I'll walk out that door,
and I'll never come back.

00:26:28.384 --> 00:26:30.761
You'll live the rest of your life...

00:26:33.904 --> 00:26:37.401
And I'll just be a bad memory.

00:27:53.094 --> 00:27:53.811
Hey!

00:28:36.044 --> 00:28:37.601
It happened...

00:28:37.604 --> 00:28:39.281
Again.

00:28:40.104 --> 00:28:41.681
Where am I?

00:28:42.514 --> 00:28:44.661
H-Help me.

00:28:45.474 --> 00:28:47.821
God. Oh, my god.

00:28:47.824 --> 00:28:50.791
Easy gelen just take it easy

00:29:20.874 --> 00:29:22.561
It should be over now.

00:29:25.374 --> 00:29:27.501
You'll never see me again.

00:29:51.514 --> 00:29:53.351
It was sort of sad, actually.

00:29:53.764 --> 00:29:56.011
Glenn had no clue what was going on.

00:29:58.534 --> 00:30:01.651
Why do you think he turned Madison
instead of just killing her?

00:30:01.654 --> 00:30:02.961
I don't know.

00:30:02.964 --> 00:30:05.171
He kind of seemed to
have a thing for her.

00:30:05.174 --> 00:30:07.641
Maybe his primal instinct did, too.

00:30:08.684 --> 00:30:12.231
Maybe he was looking for a
little hot breeding action.

00:30:12.234 --> 00:30:13.941
Yeah. Something like that.

00:30:14.844 --> 00:30:16.131
So?

00:30:17.294 --> 00:30:18.271
So what?

00:30:18.274 --> 00:30:19.951
Speaking of madison... oh, whatever.

00:30:19.954 --> 00:30:22.911
You liked her. Maybe, uh
- Dean.

00:30:22.914 --> 00:30:24.986
She thought I was a
stark-Raving lunatic.

00:30:24.989 --> 00:30:25.747
You saved her life.

00:30:25.750 --> 00:30:27.701
But she doesn't know that.

00:30:28.664 --> 00:30:32.291
You know, for a stakeout,
your car's a bit conspicous.

00:30:32.608 --> 00:30:33.791
What are you still doing here?

00:30:33.794 --> 00:30:34.841
Honestly? Uh...

00:30:36.524 --> 00:30:38.587
We're pretty sure you're
not gonna turn tonight,

00:30:38.590 --> 00:30:41.013
But we got to be 100%,

00:30:41.016 --> 00:30:43.611
So, you know, we're... lurking.

00:30:45.644 --> 00:30:48.291
Look, I know this sounds crazy
- It sure does.

00:30:50.144 --> 00:30:52.341
Well, if we're gonna wait it out...

00:30:52.604 --> 00:30:54.851
We might as well do it together.

00:31:03.674 --> 00:31:05.891
You were telling the truth, weren't you?

00:31:05.894 --> 00:31:08.061
About everything.

00:31:10.014 --> 00:31:13.151
What you did -It was to help me.

00:31:13.754 --> 00:31:15.021
Yeah.

00:31:15.024 --> 00:31:17.471
I did all those horrible things...

00:31:18.734 --> 00:31:20.681
When I turned.

00:31:22.334 --> 00:31:23.911
You didn't know.

00:31:32.394 --> 00:31:35.011
So when will we know for sure?

00:31:35.014 --> 00:31:36.971
Moonrise?  No, I don't think so.

00:31:36.974 --> 00:31:38.181
You turned middle of
the night last night.

00:31:38.184 --> 00:31:40.491
I think we got to hang in until sunup.

00:31:48.014 --> 00:31:51.031
Well, looks like we got
ourselves a few hours to kill.

00:31:51.384 --> 00:31:52.991
Poker, anyone?

00:32:16.874 --> 00:32:18.181
Oh, no, you guys talk.

00:32:34.404 --> 00:32:36.721
Does -Does this mean it worked?

00:32:36.724 --> 00:32:38.421
Yeah, I think so.

00:32:40.194 --> 00:32:42.681
Oh, god, thank you.

00:32:42.684 --> 00:32:45.561
Thank you so much.

00:32:51.184 --> 00:32:53.381
You too, Dean.

00:32:53.384 --> 00:32:54.771
Thank you.

00:32:54.774 --> 00:32:56.681
Ah, don't mention it.

00:33:00.604 --> 00:33:08.821
So, I'm just gonna head back to the hotel
and watch some pay-Per-View or something.

00:33:16.334 --> 00:33:18.051
That was smooth.

00:33:18.864 --> 00:33:20.881
He means well.

00:33:20.884 --> 00:33:24.331
He means he thinks
you're gonna get laid.

00:33:25.834 --> 00:33:27.721
Look, I --
It's okay.

00:33:27.724 --> 00:33:28.881
No.

00:33:28.884 --> 00:33:31.241
I know I scared the crap
out of you, all right?

00:33:32.394 --> 00:33:33.991
I -I mean, I tied you to a chair.

00:33:33.994 --> 00:33:37.991
That's right up there with
me scratching up your face.

00:33:40.594 --> 00:33:42.741
There's just no way...

00:33:43.424 --> 00:33:45.581
We could go back, you know?

00:33:46.834 --> 00:33:48.691
To before it happened.

00:33:48.694 --> 00:33:49.911
You're right.

00:33:50.904 --> 00:33:53.181
There's just no way.

00:35:47.124 --> 00:35:49.071
She -She turned.

00:35:49.074 --> 00:35:50.061
What?

00:35:50.064 --> 00:35:52.241
I couldn't grab her in time.

00:35:52.634 --> 00:35:54.191
We'll find her, sammy.

00:35:54.194 --> 00:35:55.811
I already called bobby.

00:35:55.814 --> 00:35:59.421
He doesn't know anything, except he knew
severing the bloodline wouldn't work.

00:35:59.424 --> 00:36:01.841
They all say it's
impossible to reverse it.

00:36:01.844 --> 00:36:03.961
How come she didn't turn
when we were with her?

00:36:03.964 --> 00:36:05.652
You put her to bed and
then she wolfed out.

00:36:05.655 --> 00:36:06.971
Maybe she's got to be asleep to turn.

00:36:06.974 --> 00:36:08.331
What the hell does it matter?

00:36:08.334 --> 00:36:10.921
We got to find some way to
help her, some legend we missed.

00:36:10.924 --> 00:36:12.691
Don't you think someone
we know would have known?

00:36:12.694 --> 00:36:15.401
Then we have to look harder
until we find something.

00:36:15.744 --> 00:36:18.651
Sammy, I don't think we
got a choice here anymore.

00:36:20.104 --> 00:36:20.851
What?

00:36:20.854 --> 00:36:23.261
She's a sweet girl, but part of her is
- Evil?

00:36:23.264 --> 00:36:23.891
Yeah.

00:36:23.894 --> 00:36:25.721
That's what they say about me, dean.

00:36:25.724 --> 00:36:29.161
So me you won't kill, but her
you're just gonna blow away?

00:36:31.644 --> 00:36:32.911
Sam?

00:36:32.914 --> 00:36:34.361
Madison, where are you?

00:36:34.364 --> 00:36:36.941
I don't -I don't -I
don't know where I am.

00:36:37.324 --> 00:36:38.971
Do you see any street signs?

00:36:38.974 --> 00:36:41.181
Um... yeah, yeah.

00:36:41.184 --> 00:36:42.671
Middle point.

00:36:42.674 --> 00:36:43.561
Hold on, maddie.

00:36:43.564 --> 00:36:45.751
We're coming to get you.
Just stay where you are.

00:36:58.004 --> 00:37:00.991
I don't remember anything.

00:37:02.714 --> 00:37:05.501
I probably killed someone last night.

00:37:06.594 --> 00:37:08.031
Didn't I?

00:37:10.894 --> 00:37:12.721
There's no way to know yet.

00:37:12.724 --> 00:37:15.561
Is there something else we
can try to make it go away?

00:37:15.564 --> 00:37:16.791
We'll find something.

00:37:16.794 --> 00:37:19.811
There's got to be
some answer -Somewhere.

00:37:19.814 --> 00:37:21.541
That's not entirely true.

00:37:21.544 --> 00:37:23.541
Madison, you deserve to know.

00:37:24.704 --> 00:37:26.911
We've scoured every source.

00:37:27.624 --> 00:37:29.381
There's just no cure.

00:37:31.704 --> 00:37:33.391
Is -Is he right?

00:37:46.774 --> 00:37:49.721
Well, we could lock
you up at night, but...

00:37:49.724 --> 00:37:52.241
You bust out, and some night you will...

00:37:53.154 --> 00:37:55.101
Someone else dies.

00:37:58.774 --> 00:38:01.141
I'm sorry. I am.

00:38:09.324 --> 00:38:12.491
So I guess that's all
there is to it, then.

00:38:13.704 --> 00:38:15.511
Stop it. Don't talk like that.

00:38:15.514 --> 00:38:17.721
Sam, I don't want to hurt anyone else.

00:38:17.724 --> 00:38:19.771
I don't want to hurt you.

00:38:27.274 --> 00:38:28.681
Put that down.

00:38:28.684 --> 00:38:31.011
I can't do it myself.

00:38:33.754 --> 00:38:36.941
I need you to help me.  Madison, no.

00:38:36.944 --> 00:38:37.951
Sam.

00:38:38.234 --> 00:38:41.191
I'm a monster. You don't have to be.

00:38:41.954 --> 00:38:44.521
We could find a way, all right?

00:38:44.524 --> 00:38:46.521
I can. I'm gonna save you.

00:38:46.524 --> 00:38:48.111
You tried.

00:38:48.114 --> 00:38:49.971
I know you tried.

00:38:50.324 --> 00:38:52.951
This is all there is left.

00:38:53.384 --> 00:38:55.111
Help me, sam.

00:38:56.264 --> 00:38:58.441
I want you to do it.

00:38:59.574 --> 00:39:01.871
I want it to be you. I can't.

00:39:01.874 --> 00:39:04.141
I don't want to die.

00:39:04.144 --> 00:39:05.901
I don't.

00:39:06.414 --> 00:39:09.091
But I can't live like this.

00:39:11.174 --> 00:39:13.851
This is the way you can save me.

00:39:15.474 --> 00:39:17.641
Please.

00:39:19.114 --> 00:39:22.101
I'm asking you to save me.

00:40:17.104 --> 00:40:18.681
Sam

00:40:27.384 --> 00:40:28.441
I'm sorry.

00:40:28.444 --> 00:40:30.021
No, you're right.

00:40:31.324 --> 00:40:33.561
She's right.

00:40:34.844 --> 00:40:36.621
Sammy, I got this one. I'll do it.

00:40:36.624 --> 00:40:38.641
She asked me to.

00:40:39.614 --> 00:40:42.671
You don't have to. Yes, I do.

00:40:47.684 --> 00:40:49.541
Please.

00:40:58.884 --> 00:41:01.121
Just wait here.



00:01:46.654 --> 00:01:48.154
